Product fix (REL-6 DISCONNECT class first finding): a mid-run kill leaves an in-flight ActionEvent permanently without its paired observation — the durable event log then carries a dangling action forever. Evidence: disconnect_cancel_recovery soak run failed EventChainOracle ACTION_NO_OBSERVATION after cancel_at killed mid-write. Dangling pairs are exactly what REL-RC-K showed poisons provider history rendering on later resume.
Fix in packages/agent-server runtime kill path (runtime.kill / the executor teardown it triggers): before/while terminalizing a killed conversation, find any ActionEvent in the log without a paired ObservationEvent/AgentErrorEvent (pairing by action_id — reuse the pairing helpers from signals/_successful_action_ids or finish.py) and append an AgentErrorEvent(error="cancelled", detail="action cancelled by kill switch before completing", action_id=<id>, tool_call_id=<call id>) for each — closing the pair honestly. Must be idempotent (a second kill doesn't double-append) and only cover actions from the CURRENT run segment (seq after the last terminal/plan boundary is fine — simplest honest scope: any dangling action in the whole log lacking closure, since closure is idempotent by action_id check).
Tests: kill with in-flight action -> log gains exactly one cancelled AgentErrorEvent paired to it; second kill no-op; kill with no dangling actions appends nothing; EventChainOracle passes over a killed+recovered event sequence (use the harness normalize/oracle directly in a test if importable, else assert pairing invariant).
